From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: d4r <d4r@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] FSR FG input: aspect ratio from the display size when generationRect is empty

FSR frame generation passes a generationRect of 0x0 to mean the whole swapchain (Ghost of Tsushima does). The
PREPARE handlers divided that width by that height for the camera aspect ratio, 0 / 0 = NaN, and the NaN went into
DLSSG's constants (cameraAspectRatio) with all-zero projection matrices, every frame: artifacts in the generated
frames. Use the context's display size, then the swapchain size, when the rect is empty.
---
diff --git a/OptiScaler/inputs/FG/FfxApi_Dx12_FG.cpp b/OptiScaler/inputs/FG/FfxApi_Dx12_FG.cpp
index b303eebd..dffa6b85 100644
--- a/OptiScaler/inputs/FG/FfxApi_Dx12_FG.cpp
+++ b/OptiScaler/inputs/FG/FfxApi_Dx12_FG.cpp
@@ -1088,7 +1088,14 @@ ffxReturnCode_t ffxDispatch_Dx12FG(ffxContext* context, ffxDispatchDescHeader* d
         UINT64 dispWidth = 0;
         UINT dispHeight = 0;
         fg->GetInterpolationRect(dispWidth, dispHeight, fIndex);
-        auto aspectRatio = (float) dispWidth / (float) dispHeight;
+        if (dispWidth == 0 || dispHeight == 0)
+        {
+            // A generationRect of 0x0 means the whole swapchain. Without this the aspect ratio below is 0 / 0 = NaN,
+            // which reached DLSSG as cameraAspectRatio and kept its projection matrices from being built.
+            dispWidth = _fgConst.displayWidth != 0 ? _fgConst.displayWidth : s.currentSwapchainDesc.BufferDesc.Width;
+            dispHeight = _fgConst.displayHeight != 0 ? _fgConst.displayHeight : s.currentSwapchainDesc.BufferDesc.Height;
+        }
+        auto aspectRatio = dispHeight != 0 ? (float) dispWidth / (float) dispHeight : 16.0f / 9.0f;
         fg->SetCameraValues(cdDesc->cameraNear, cdDesc->cameraFar, cdDesc->cameraFovAngleVertical, aspectRatio, 0.0f,
                             fIndex);
 
@@ -1180,7 +1187,14 @@ ffxReturnCode_t ffxDispatch_Dx12FG(ffxContext* context, ffxDispatchDescHeader* d
         UINT64 dispWidth = 0;
         UINT dispHeight = 0;
         fg->GetInterpolationRect(dispWidth, dispHeight, fIndex);
-        auto aspectRatio = (float) dispWidth / (float) dispHeight;
+        if (dispWidth == 0 || dispHeight == 0)
+        {
+            // A generationRect of 0x0 means the whole swapchain. Without this the aspect ratio below is 0 / 0 = NaN,
+            // which reached DLSSG as cameraAspectRatio and kept its projection matrices from being built.
+            dispWidth = _fgConst.displayWidth != 0 ? _fgConst.displayWidth : s.currentSwapchainDesc.BufferDesc.Width;
+            dispHeight = _fgConst.displayHeight != 0 ? _fgConst.displayHeight : s.currentSwapchainDesc.BufferDesc.Height;
+        }
+        auto aspectRatio = dispHeight != 0 ? (float) dispWidth / (float) dispHeight : 16.0f / 9.0f;
         fg->SetCameraValues(cdDesc->cameraNear, cdDesc->cameraFar, cdDesc->cameraFovAngleVertical, aspectRatio, 0.0f,
                             fIndex);
 
